<title>FRANCE: Jacques Fath fashion house names Russian designer.</title>
<headline>Jacques Fath fashion house names Russian designer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French fashion house Jacques Fath said on Thursday it had named 27-year-old Russian designer Elena Nazaroff to design its ready-to-wear collection.</p>
<p>The appointment of the Moscow-born Nazaroff, who studied at the Parsons School of Design in New York City, follows last March's acquisition of Jacques Fath by EK Finances.</p>
<p>Nazaroff replaces Tom Van Lingen.</p>
<p>EK Finances, a French firm grouping the Emmanuelle Khanh fashion house and Harel shoes, bought the Jean-Louis Scherrer fashion house last week from Japanese retail giant Seibu.</p>
</text>
